Open the spreadsheet program (for example Microsoft Excel) and start a blank workbook. Type the data exactly as in Figure 2, cell by cell:

- **A1**: `Mock Exam Results - 2009` (the title);
- **row 2** (column headers): `S/n`, `Students Names`, `Sex`, `Eng`, `Fre`, `Mat`, `His`, `Geo`, `Econs` in cells A2 to I2;
- **rows 3 to 12**: one student per row, S/n 1 to 10 in column A, the name in B, the sex (M or F) in C and the marks out of 20 in D to I. Leave the cell **empty** where the figure shows no mark (Njie Fabian in His, Verla Jones in Mat, Akemjia Leonard in His).

Marks are typed as numbers (decimals with a point, such as 11.5). Then *File* > *Save As* with the name **Task 2** (see question 5). The marks of the data entry reward the exact content of the 11 rows and of the title.
